#!/usr/bin/python3
"""omakeylog capture engine.

Counts how often each key, each adjacent key-pair and each short key sequence
is pressed, so the data can drive a QMK keymap (home-row placement, thumb and
layer keys, less finger travel, home-row-mod timing).

Privacy: it stores ONLY aggregate numbers - per-key, per-pair, per-skip-pair,
per-triple and per-shortcut counts, plus histograms of how long keys are held.
It never keeps an ordered log of keypresses, never timestamps individual keys,
and never records which window had focus, so the typed text cannot be
reconstructed from what it writes.

Subcommands:
  record [--device PATH ...] [--foreground]   start counting (daemonizes)
  resume                                       start again if it was recording
                                               before a reboot or logout
  stop                                         stop the running recorder
  status                                       print JSON status
  report [--json | --csv] [--no-compare]       analyse stats for QMK
  reset                                        back up and clear the counts
  layout show                                  print the key -> finger mapping
  layout import-vil FILE [--right-inner-first] build a layout from a Vial file
  layout reset                                 go back to the QWERTY mapping

Data lives in ~/.local/share/omakeylog/, the optional custom layout in
~/.config/omakeylog/layout.json.
"""

